{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_three_tier_model", "label": "The three-tier model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "AI is not the only option, and treating it as the only option is the failure mode; AI does the smallest job only AI can do."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_tier_1_deterministic", "label": "Tier 1 \u2014 deterministic AST transform", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "XSJS is ES5 plus the $ global so acorn parses it cleanly; typed transforms cover imports, DB collapse, request/response, direct substitutions, SQL fixes and async propagation \u2014 the last derived over the call graph, not guessed, which is exactly what the hand migration got wrong."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_tier_2_ai_fills_holes", "label": "Tier 2 \u2014 AI fills holes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two things changed in the building, both in the same direction: the model returns one word per interpolated SQL value rather than code, and the answer re-enters the analysis rather than the file, so it must pass the same bar as a statement no model ever saw."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_tier_3_human", "label": "Tier 3 \u2014 human", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Anything Tier 2 returns that fails validation twice."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_hole", "label": "Hole (a marked unresolved node)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything Tier 1 cannot decide becomes a hole carrying the NEO excerpt, the reason, and the surrounding converted context."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_artifact_taxonomy", "label": "The complete artifact taxonomy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Counted from disk, not from documentation. Only three types carry JavaScript, so the 'AI problem' is ~12% of in-scope files \u2014 scoping it correctly stops AI leaking into the other 88%."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_closed_set_xsjs_api", "label": "The XSJS API surface is a closed set", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The single most important fact in the document: XSJS is not an open-ended language problem but a small, fixed, enumerable API of about 15 idioms, all with a known target form."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_launders_mechanical_into_probabilistic", "label": "Laundering a mechanical transform into a probabilistic one", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Handing the model every unresolved finding spends tokens on work a parser already does deterministically and converts a mechanical transform into a probabilistic one \u2014 the tempting failure mode."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_jdbc_chain_collapse", "label": "JDBC chain collapse to await cds.run", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recognised by data flow, not text: getConnection \u2192 prepareStatement \u2192 setX \u2192 executeQuery \u2192 next loop \u2192 getX, with array-vs-object decided from the statement kind rather than from memory."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_positional_column_access", "label": "Positional column access (897 getX(N), zero by name)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolving getInteger(3) requires parsing the SELECT list; a parser does it identically every time, a model has to infer it, and when it is wrong the code still runs and returns the wrong column. This is the strongest argument for a deterministic transform and against handing files to a model."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_checklist_item_16", "label": "Checklist item 16 \u2014 result object vs array", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A SELECT yields an array; a CALL with OUT params yields an object. The tool knows because it is converting the .hdbprocedure files in the same run, so the signature is a fact in hand. The shipped hand migration got this wrong twice in one file."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_reference_bugs", "label": "Bugs in the hand-migrated reference", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Worth naming because the tool must not learn from them: a SELECT result bound as a scalar, result.USERCOUNT without the [0], and a silent behaviour change in the simplest file in the corpus. This is what 'hand the file to a model and ask it to convert' produces."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_function_level_unit", "label": "The unit is the function, not the file", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Files reach 25-49 KB so one prompt has no verification granularity and blows a local model's context; file-level also discards everything Tier 1 already proved. A function is coherent, verifiable (name, arity, return shape), small, recoverable in one retry, and parallelisable."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_facts_block", "label": "The FACTS block", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The model's biggest failure mode is inventing names, so the prompt asserts as fact everything already known \u2014 resolved imports, real table names, procedure signatures and OUT-vs-result-set, the function's call sites. Anything not in FACTS must be flagged rather than invented."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_deterministic_gate", "label": "The deterministic gate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A model's answer is a proposal; it must pass a deterministic gate. The model is a suggestion engine inside a deterministic pipeline, never writes a file directly, and its output faces the same checks as Tier 1's."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_task_registry", "label": "Task registry (task-specific prompts, not one convert prompt)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One generic instruction is what large models tolerate and small models fail; each task gets its own tight prompt, output shape and validator (sql-fold, column-resolve, chain-collapse, req-boundary, body-convert). Most return a fragment or JSON, not code, which is what makes a 7B model viable."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_small_local_model_design", "label": "Designing for a small local model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Target the small-model case rather than treat it as a downgrade: the remaining tasks are local pattern transformation with the facts supplied. Small models are worse at declining, so 'flag rather than guess' must be enforced by the pipeline, not requested in the prompt \u2014 never accept output merely because it parses."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_retrieval_few_shot", "label": "The corpus as a retrieval few-shot bank", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "209 matched NEO\u2192CF pairs give real before/after examples; a small model with one on-domain example beats a large model with none. The pairs are also the actual eval \u2014 HumanEval and SWE-bench measure agentic multi-file coding and do not transfer."}, {"id": "docs_conversion_strategy_sql_fold", "label": "Statically foldable concatenation (sql-fold)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Most of the 109 concatenation sites have every operand as a literal or an expression node, so folding into a template with ? binds is an AST transform, not a reasoning task \u2014 Tier 2's real residue is tens of sites, not hundreds."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_three_tier_model", "target": "docs_conversion_strategy_tier_1_deterministic", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_three_tier_model", "target": "docs_conversion_strategy_tier_2_ai_fills_holes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_three_tier_model", "target": "docs_conversion_strategy_tier_3_human", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_tier_1_deterministic", "target": "src_transform_file_transformfile", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_tier_1_deterministic", "target": "src_transform_imports_importedits", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_tier_1_deterministic", "target": "src_transform_request_requestedits", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_tier_1_deterministic", "target": "src_transform_emitdb_propagateasync", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 async propagation", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_jdbc_chain_collapse", "target": "src_transform_db_analysedb", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_jdbc_chain_collapse", "target": "src_transform_emitdb_dbedits", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_positional_column_access", "target": "src_transform_db_selectcolumns", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_positional_column_access", "target": "src_transform_db_aliasunnamedcolumns", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_checklist_item_16", "target": "src_parse_procsig_lookupprocedure", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_checklist_item_16", "target": "src_transform_db_statementkind", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a74 array-vs-object from statement kind", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_reference_bugs", "target": "docs_conversion_strategy_checklist_item_16", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/CONVERSION-STRATEGY.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_conversion_strategy_reference_bugs", "tar